The Zion Gate is closed.  Move along, infidel, and I mean NOW!	錫安城門已經關閉。滾開，異教徒，我說的是現在！
The Zion gate is closed.  You should consider yourself fortunate if we allow you to leave with your skin intact.	錫安城門已經關閉。若我們容你毫髮無傷地離開，你便該心懷感激。
It is a long way to the bottom of the hill!	到山腳還有好長一段路！
The wall is too thick and the opening too narrow to see anything inside.	牆壁太厚，開口太窄，看不見裡頭的情形。
Why would you insult an armed group of men?  Are you feeling exceptionally suicidal today?	你為何要出言侮辱一群全副武裝的人？難道你今天特別想尋死？
We have moved as far as we will move.  Do not push your luck, dog of an infidel.	我們已經讓到頭了，不會再退。休得得寸進尺，異教狗。
There is a dangerous looking Mercenary guard and his thugs guarding a small, closed gate.  They outnumber you, Arthur, and they are well armed.	一名面露凶光的傭兵守衛與他的爪牙，看守著一道緊閉的小門。亞瑟，他們人數多於你，而且裝備精良。
These thugs have the look of violence about them.	這些爪牙渾身透著一股凶悍之氣。
The mercenary's evil eyes are filled with a savage bloodlust.  He enjoys killing as much as he enjoys taking money	這名傭兵的雙眼透著凶殘嗜血之色，殺人取樂與圖財害命，於他而言不相上下
Now that he has been paid, the mercenary eyes you with contempt.	如今傭兵已經拿到了錢，只以輕蔑的眼神看你。
The large Mercenary in the pale blue robe is obviously the leader of this little band of thugs.	那個身披淺藍長袍的高大傭兵，顯然是這群爪牙的頭目。
These men carry scimitars, a most lethal Arab weapon.	這些人佩帶彎刀，是阿拉伯人最致命的武器。
Do not be fooled by the look of cloth.  They could well have a helmet beneath the turban.	別被那身布料的外表騙了，頭巾底下很可能藏著頭盔。
Their robes may look strange to us, but they are perfectly suited to this climate.	他們的長袍在我們眼中或許顯得古怪，卻十分適合這裡的氣候。
You may have to pay them again.   Let us hope not.	你或許還得再付他們一次錢，但願不必如此。
Let us hope that they will not wish payment to let you leave Jerusalem.	但願他們不會要你付錢才肯放你離開耶路撒冷。
You were very wise to avoid a fight with four heavily armed and dangerous men.	避開與四名全副武裝的凶悍男子交手，是明智之舉。
You are a lone foreigner against four dangerous mercenaries.  Your life is worth far more than a few coins.	你孤身一人，對上四名凶悍的傭兵。你的性命遠比幾枚錢幣更加珍貴。
I do hope you can talk your way out of this, Arthur, but I fear the only language they speak is that of money.	亞瑟，我衷心希望你能靠三言兩語脫身，但恐怕他們只聽得懂金錢這種語言。
The discs seem to be a part of the walls, but I cannot say what their purpose may be.	這些圓盤似乎是城牆的一部分，但我說不出它們的用途。
It is an archiere, from which arrows can be fired in time of war.	那是一處箭孔，戰時可從中射箭。
The door handles are made of iron.	門把是鐵製的。
You cannot see it from here.  It is in the western wall.	從這裡看不見，它在西邊的城牆上。
If I read my maps of Jerusalem correctly, this is called the Zion Gate and is a minor gate in the south wall.	若我沒看錯耶路撒冷的地圖，此處喚作錫安城門，是南面城牆上的一道小門。
The arch is part of the structure of the Gate.	這道拱門是城門結構的一部分。
These spiny plants are Aloe Vera.	這些帶刺的植物是蘆薈。
The walls of Jerusalem are made of huge blocks of a buff-colored stone.	耶路撒冷的城牆由巨大的淺黃色石塊砌成。
Aye, they are rocks.  There is a lot of rock in this country.	正是，這些是岩石。這片土地上岩石多得很。
Arthur, are you mad?!	亞瑟，你瘋了嗎？！
The walls of Jerusalem continue on as far as you can see.	耶路撒冷的城牆一路延伸，望不到盡頭。
It is a long way to the bottom of the hill.	到山腳還有好長一段路。
You have reached one corner of the walls of Jerusalem.  The mercenaries back at the Zion Gate watch you warily.	你來到了耶路撒冷城牆的一角。錫安城門那邊的傭兵正警戒地盯著你。
Another stretch of ancient wall awaits you.	眼前又是一段古老的城牆。
To the north is the Jaffa Gate.	北邊是賈法城門。
There is something ahead that may be the Jaffa Gate.	前方似乎有什麼東西，可能是賈法城門。
To the south is the southwest corner of the walls of Jerusalem.	南邊是耶路撒冷城牆的西南角。
Aye, 'tis a scrubby tree of no great interest.	正是，這是一株矮小的灌木，沒什麼看頭。
He smells as though he has been sleeping in a pen of goats.  It is a good thing that you are standing upwind.	他身上的氣味，彷彿睡在羊圈裡似的。幸好你站在上風處。
I warn you, I am an official of the city!  Pay me an entrance fee or go away.	我警告你，我是本城的官吏！付入城費，不然就滾開。
Come, come, I do not have all day.  You must pay me a fee to enter the Jaffa Gate.  Whatever you can afford.	來吧來吧，我可沒空耗一整天。你得付費才能進賈法城門，多少都行，隨你的能力。
He did not seem to hear you. Perhaps you are too far away.	他似乎沒聽見你的話，或許你離得太遠了。
If you lay hands upon me, I will call for the city guards and they will chop you into little pieces.	你若敢對我動手，我便叫城衛來，他們會把你剁成碎片。
May the fleas of a thousand camels infest your tent!	願千頭駱駝的跳蚤，都鑽進你的帳篷！
He does not seem to hear you.	他似乎沒聽見你的話。
He is dirty, has a disreputable look, and his clothes are old, threadbare, and smell of goats.	他一身骯髒，模樣不端，衣衫破舊，還帶著羊臊味。
A thicket of bushes blocks the path to the north.	一叢灌木擋住了通往北方的路。
He is gone, good riddance.	他走了，走了也好。
He will know the escape routes of this city.  I doubt that you will have a chance to catch up with him.	他必然熟知這座城的脫身路線，我不認為你追得上他。
Arthur!  Will you PLEASE show some caution with the few possessions you have left.	亞瑟！你剩下沒幾件家當了，拜託小心一點好嗎！
Ridiculous!  The last thing on earth you need is a brainless sheep.	荒唐！你這輩子最不需要的，就是一頭沒腦子的羊。
Perhaps one of the merchants inside would be interested.	或許裡頭有哪位商人會感興趣。
This is the Jaffa Gate.  What are you waiting for?  Enter.	這是賈法城門，你還在等什麼？進去吧。
I suppose there are plenty of merchants in the bazaar.	我想市集裡商人多得是。
Aye, he was a fraud if I ever saw one.	正是，他要不是騙子，我這輩子就沒見過騙子。
Aye, Arthur, you must be wary of thieves.	正是，亞瑟，你得提防竊賊。
There is a shop selling cloth inside the bazaar.	市集裡有間賣布的鋪子。
He is gone, and good riddance.	他走了，走了也好。
The woman and her sheep are gone.	那婦人與她的羊都不見了。
This must be the Jaffa Gate.  There is a glimpse of the local bazaar inside, with an open gutter that runs down the center of the street.	這想必就是賈法城門了。門內可以窺見當地的市集，一條露天水溝沿著街道中央流淌。
Not to mention this bothersome man who is determined to have words with you.	更別提這個死纏著要跟你搭話的討厭傢伙了。
It is the Jaffa Gate and the way is open.	這是賈法城門，門是開著的。
You must pay me a fee to enter the Jaffa Gate.  Whatever you can afford, but you must pay.	你得付費才能進賈法城門，多少隨你，但一定得付。
Hey, you!	喂，你！
Yes, yes, welcome to Jerusalem.  Now pay me the fee to enter and let us be done with it.	好好，歡迎來到耶路撒冷。現在付入城費吧，咱們好把這事了結。
There is a rather interesting smell of frying food drifting out of the Jaffa Gate.	賈法城門飄出一股頗誘人的煎炸食物香氣。
Without the smell of goat interfering, there is a rather interesting smell of frying food drifting out of the Jaffa Gate.	少了那股羊臊味的干擾，賈法城門飄出的煎炸食物香氣顯得格外誘人。
Ah, uh, no, a mule is too difficult to deal with.  Just money will do.	啊，呃，不了，騾子太麻煩了，給錢就行。
No, no, YOU must pay ME to enter the gate.	不，不，是「你」得付錢給「我」才能進這城門。
No, no, you must give me money, not sell me something.	不不，你得給我錢，不是要賣我東西。
We are reasonable here.  Whatever you can afford.  Come on, I do not have all day.	我們這裡通情達理，多少隨你的能力。來吧，我可沒空耗一整天。
Ahm...uhmm...I know nothing of any thief!	呃……嗯……我對什麼竊賊一無所知！
Yasser likes not the flash of your steel.	亞西爾不喜歡看見你亮出鋼刃。
That has set the fraud to his heels.  But you had best put up your sword for now.  There may be more guards like those at the Zion gate.	這下讓那騙子拔腿就跑了。但你此刻最好還是收起劍——這附近說不定還有像錫安城門那樣的守衛。
By my beard, Arthur, I believe he was a fraud.	憑我這把鬍子起誓，亞瑟，我看他就是個騙子。
The road leads back into the desert.	這條路通回沙漠。
My advice is simple and obvious.  Enter Jerusalem and search for the Grail!	我的建議簡單明瞭：進入耶路撒冷，尋找聖杯！
There's no one here to attack.	這裡沒有人可以攻擊。
The road seems to stretch on forever.	這條路彷彿沒有盡頭。
It is a scrubby and uninteresting tree.	這是一株矮小平凡的樹，沒什麼看頭。
In the distance is the searing desert and arid hills through which you have journeyed.	遠方是你一路走過的灼熱沙漠與乾旱丘陵。
It cannot be seen from here.	從這裡看不見。
The walls of Jerusalem are but a few paces away.	耶路撒冷的城牆只在幾步之遙。
Behind you, the Jaffa Gate is open and Jerusalem awaits you.	你身後，賈法城門敞開著，耶路撒冷正等著你。
Concern yourself with your sacred mission.  That is all that matters.	把心思放在你神聖的使命上，那才是唯一要緊的事。
Arthur, halt!  At great cost to myself, I send this vision of warning.  You must not turn away from your mission now.	亞瑟，止步！我耗費莫大的心力，才將這個警示的異象傳給你。此刻，你絕不能背離你的使命。
Months of weary labor and travel have brought you here.  There is nothing this way but the desert whose hardship you have already suffered.	數月的艱辛跋涉，才將你帶到此地。這條路上除了你已經受過的沙漠苦難，再無他物。
Turn back to Jerusalem, King Arthur, and seek your destiny within.	回頭吧，亞瑟王，回耶路撒冷去，在城中尋得你的命運。
So, in spite of my best efforts and advice, you insist on heading back into the desert like an utter fool.	看來，不顧我竭盡全力的勸告，你仍執意像個十足的傻子那樣，一頭栽回沙漠裡去。
And to think that men once hailed you as King and praised your ability.	想想看，曾經有人尊你為王，讚頌你的才能。
The guards remain and will not let you leave. Do not annoy them, Arthur. There are many more of them and they are all well armed.	守衛仍守在那裡，不會放你離開。亞瑟，別去招惹他們，他們人數眾多，而且裝備精良。
In Latin, the sign reads "Arma" meaning weaponry or armour. Mohammed is the name of the merchant.	以拉丁文寫著「Arma」，意為武器或盔甲。商人的名字是穆罕默德。
The Islamic symbols above his name are the crescent moon and a scimitar. The rest is in Arabic.	他名字上方的伊斯蘭符號是一彎新月與一把彎刀，其餘部分則是阿拉伯文。
It is difficult to see through the shutters.	百葉窗擋著，很難看清裡頭。
My, quite a view.	哎呀，好一片景致。
The second floor of this building has a window and a balcony.	這棟建築的二樓有一扇窗與一座陽台。
Across the street are more merchants.	街道對面還有更多商人。
The weapons shop is closed.	武器店關著門。
There is nothing more to be gained here. Do as she instructs.	這裡已經沒有更多可得的了，照她說的做吧。
There is now a girl crying in front of Mohammed's shop. And see, her doves have escaped.	此刻有個女孩在穆罕默德的店前哭泣，你看，她的鴿子都逃走了。
Mohammed's shop may be closed, but it appears Mari is open for business.	穆罕默德的店雖然關著，但瑪麗似乎正在營業。
The weapon merchant's shop is closed.	武器商人的店關著門。
Your mule is being held safely by the weapons merchant. You are fortunate he is an honest man.	你的騾子安然由武器商人代為看管，幸好他是個誠實的人。
The weapons merchant looks sympathetic. I suspect this is not the first time he has seen this thief in action.	武器商人一臉同情的神色，我猜這已不是他第一次見識那竊賊的手法。
The scimitar is a common Islamic emblem.	彎刀是常見的伊斯蘭象徵。
The crescent moon is a symbol of the Goddess.	新月是女神的象徵。
It is dark inside and you can see nothing.	裡頭一片漆黑，你什麼也看不見。
The windows downstairs are closed. One of the windows upstairs is closed.	樓下的窗戶關著，樓上也有一扇窗戶關著。
It is closed.	它關著。
There is no way up to it from here.	從這裡沒有路可以上去。
There are no stairs.	這裡沒有樓梯。
Aye, they are rocks.	正是，這些是岩石。
Watch for him if you like, but I doubt he will come near you again.	你若想留意他也行，但我不認為他還敢靠近你。
He is gone, as you can see.	如你所見，他已經走了。
A dubious tactic at best.	這頂多算是個可疑的招數。
First you must get her attention.	你得先引起她的注意。
She is not here.	她不在這裡。
She is gone.	她已經離開了。
These rocks are too heavy for any practical use.	這些石頭太重，派不上什麼實際用場。
The door is locked.	門鎖著。
No one answers.	沒有人應門。
You would not need to, even if the weapons merchant were here.	就算武器商人在這裡，你也用不著這麼做。
And be mistaken for a thief?! Do not be a fool. Besides, you could find nothing better than Excaliber, even in this shop.	還被人誤認成竊賊？！別犯傻了。再說，就算在這間店裡，你也找不到比聖劍更好的東西。
Totally impractical with all your gear, not to mention how it might excite the city guards.	帶著你這一身裝備，那根本不切實際，更別提會引來城衛的注意了。
You should have paid more attention to the scroll in my room before you left Camelot.	你離開肯萊特之前，該多留心我房裡那卷卷軸才是。
Why do you waste time here?	你何必在這裡浪費時間？
Remember, you are dealing with Arab money now. A fals is a copper coin. 4 fals are worth a dirham which is silver. 4 dirhams equal a dinar, which is gold.	記住，如今你打交道的是阿拉伯貨幣。法爾斯（fals）是銅幣，四枚法爾斯抵一枚銀幣迪爾罕（dirham）；四枚迪爾罕則等於一枚金幣第納爾（dinar）。
No answer. Perhaps she is not home.	沒有回應，或許她不在家。
She does not answer.	她沒有回應。
Across the street is a weapons shop.	街道對面是一間武器店。
The felafel seller does business as usual. Ibrahim has still not returned, however.	賣法拉費的攤販一如往常做著生意，然而易布拉興依舊沒有回來。
